1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:02,710
[horse galloping]

2
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:05,460
♪

3
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,250
[ANNE]
Challe.

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,210
[LAFALLE]
What's wrong?

5
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:18,250
Are you cold?
Shh!

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,080
We're nearly there.

7
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,130
[CHALLE] All right,
we've come far enough.

8
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,170
Now, let Anne go.

9
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:05,380
She can't run away
from here alone

10
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,750
and you've got my wing
in your hands,

11
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:10,420
so there's no escaping.

12
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,920
As much as I would like
to prolong your torment,

13
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,880
it might make you so furious
that you would

14
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,580
never come back from it.

15
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:20,830
[Anne groans]

16
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,710
[Anne shivering]

17
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:29,250
Lafalle. She's freezing.
We need a fireplace.

18
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,420
Very well,
allow me to show you the way.

19
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,330
♪

20
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,750
[shuddering]

21
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:55,670
[sighs]

22
00:02:57,330 --> 00:02:58,670
[ANNE]
Thank you, Challe.

23
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,210
That helps.

24
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:03,750
So our friends
and all our work.

25
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:06,170
D'you think they're safe?

26
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:10,000
And what about your wing?

27
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:11,960
[CHALLE]
It's fine.

28
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,920
Just forget all that for now.

29
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:18,080
I'm sure you're weary.

30
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:22,040
So rest.
You aren't working tomorrow.

31
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:24,670
Try to get some sleep.

32
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:26,670
♪

33
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,670
Stop it!

34
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,580
[whimpers]

35
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:43,960
Hm?

36
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,880
Flames are lovely,
don't you agree?

37
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:51,460
When I first saw humans

38
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,460
burning things
inside their houses.

39
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:56,540
I assumed that it was
only done for decoration.

40
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:59,500
But then I was surprised
to learn

41
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:00,880
that it was for survival.

42
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:03,830
They're so weak, aren't they?

43
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:07,130
Humans were originally
barbaric creatures.

44
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:09,250
Unsightly animals
with no wisdom

45
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:11,130
or strength to speak of.

46
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:14,580
So, naturally those filthy curs
admired us.

47
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,000
They adored us so much

48
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,130
that they began
to develop fairy-like forms

49
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:20,330
and slightly grow
more intelligent.

50
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:24,750
But they are nothing like us.

51
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:27,710
[CHALLE]
Get out.

52
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,210
[LAFALLE] I've prepared
a separate room for you.

53
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,920
It's not shabby and sparse
like this one.

54
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:36,830
After all, someone like you
belongs right next to me.

55
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:40,380
[CHALLE] You speak as though
you weren't squeezing my wing

56
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:42,000
in your hand before.

57
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:44,460
I would be glad to give it back

58
00:04:44,790 --> 00:04:47,210
as long as you were prepared
to live alongside me

59
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,750
for the rest of your days.

60
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:51,000
There are warrior fairies here.

61
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,040
What purpose do they serve?

62
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:56,250
Follow me.

63
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,670
[LAFALLE]
The previous fairy king

64
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,920
tried to understand humans.

65
00:05:04,330 --> 00:05:06,710
But the human king, Cedric,

66
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,710
instigated war against him.

67
00:05:09,290 --> 00:05:11,040
That fact alone
ought to be proof

68
00:05:11,130 --> 00:05:14,380
that fairies and humans
are fundamentally incompatible.

69
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:15,540
What is your point?

70
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:17,880
You do know it, don't you?

71
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,000
The name of the fairy king.

72
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,500
Riselva Cyril Sash.

73
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:28,630
Exactly the one
who gave us life.

74
00:05:29,250 --> 00:05:30,420
[LAFALLE]
The owner of the sword

75
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,460
inlaid
with the precious stones.

76
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:37,040
Opal. Obsidian. Diamond.

77
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:41,000
In Riselva's Cyril Sash's eyes,

78
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:43,420
each of those gems
held great potential.

79
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,000
He hoped that one of them

80
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,540
would give birth
to the next fairy king.

81
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,330
You mean?

82
00:05:50,290 --> 00:05:52,500
[EARL OF DOWNING] Anne Halford
has been abducted, you say?

83
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:56,040
Yes. I received word
from the Paige Workshop.

84
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,330
She was taken away by the fairy

85
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:00,580
who's been attacking
sugar artisans.

86
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:02,920
Others were injured, as well.

87
00:06:03,710 --> 00:06:06,790
In light of this the festival's
a lost cause for them.

88
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:10,750
Then double the guards
at once.

89
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,710
[CHALLE]
The fairy king?

90
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,920
What makes you think
I'd believe that?

91
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,170
And even if it were true,

92
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:21,130
Riselva's sword was put
under the humans' protection.

93
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:24,500
No one wants the birth
of a new fairy king,

94
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:25,710
and you know that.

95
00:06:26,290 --> 00:06:29,250
Well, no humans do.

96
00:06:30,710 --> 00:06:33,170
[LAFALLE]
And yet, you and I were born.

97
00:06:34,130 --> 00:06:36,630
I was gazed upon
by a moon eagle.

98
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:41,920
And you came to life
because of a young girl.

99
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:43,750
♪

100
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:50,500
However,
none of it was coincidence.

101
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:54,630
The fairy king had arranged
these destinies for us.

102
00:06:57,330 --> 00:06:59,920
All these years later,
there's no sign

103
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,330
that our kin will be born
from the diamond.

104
00:07:02,790 --> 00:07:05,540
In the end,
even though the fairy king

105
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:07,750
entrusted his legacy
to one of three,

106
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,830
only you and I were born.

107
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:14,210
And then,
after so much time apart,

108
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,290
I happened to find you.

109
00:07:17,210 --> 00:07:18,880
We were fated to meet.

110
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:21,130
Don't you understand?

111
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:24,540
You and I are both so powerful.

112
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:27,130
Together we can set
all of the fairies free!

113
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,500
Then we can carry on
Riselva's will

114
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:32,420
and reclaim this kingdom
for our own kind!

115
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,790
Freedom. I see.

116
00:07:41,290 --> 00:07:42,460
I refuse.

117
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:45,040
If that's what you want,
do it yourself.

118
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,920
Even if it is
what Riselva intended,

119
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:50,630
I still have no interest
in the fairy king.

120
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,960
[grunts]

121
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:57,380
[LAFALLE] Even after learning
the reason you were born?

122
00:07:57,630 --> 00:08:00,670
That's for me to decide,
not Riselva.

123
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:07,290
This is because of that girl.

124
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:08,880
That little wretch.

125
00:08:09,170 --> 00:08:12,040
To think that she has stolen
your heart so completely!

126
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,170
[grunts]

127
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,000
Don't you dare touch Anne!

128
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:17,420
I will cut you down!

129
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:19,540
I swear it!

130
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:21,170
[LAFALLE]
Are you sure you can?

131
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:23,130
You'll cut your wing
in the process.

132
00:08:23,210 --> 00:08:26,330
If it means that you'll die,
then we'll die together.

133
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:29,710
You truly are devoted to her.

134
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:31,710
Very well.

135
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:34,130
In that case,
the next fairy king...

136
00:08:35,710 --> 00:08:37,790
- will be me.
- [Challe grunts]

137
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,290
[LAFALLE]
But remember,

138
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:41,540
no matter how attached
you are to her,

139
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:44,420
she'll only bring
you both unhappiness.

140
00:08:44,710 --> 00:08:46,290
[CHALLE]
What do you mean?

141
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:47,960
[LAFALLE]
You'll be fine.

142
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:51,080
Obsidian fairies
live long lives, after all.

143
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:53,040
So, you can seek
comfort from her

144
00:08:53,130 --> 00:08:55,250
until the moment
her life runs out.

145
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,290
But think of Anne!

146
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:01,960
She will devote the entirety
of her life to caring for you

147
00:09:02,130 --> 00:09:04,580
and leave no other mark
on this world.

148
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:09,080
When seeking someone
to share their lives,

149
00:09:09,290 --> 00:09:11,250
humans are better off
with humans.

150
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,750
And it's only natural
for fairies

151
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:16,380
to spend their lives
with their own kind.

152
00:09:18,210 --> 00:09:19,420
Mark my words,

153
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:21,960
you'll cause her nothing
but sorrow.

154
00:09:23,670 --> 00:09:25,750
[horse galloping]

155
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,750
[KIETH] The Paige Workshop
was attacked?

156
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:32,000
[MARCUS] There's a message
from the Viscount.

157
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,040
The master's stand-in was hurt

158
00:09:34,130 --> 00:09:36,040
and the Head of Artisans
was abducted,

159
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:38,540
along with the warrior fairy
who had traveled with her.

160
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:40,630
[Kieth gasps]
But that means...

161
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,630
Forgive me.
I need to go there!

162
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,040
- [MARCUS] Wait.
- [KIETH] Hm?

163
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,880
[MARCUS]
You know you won't be welcome.

164
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,170
Have you forgotten?

165
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,500
[KIETH]
No, but still. I have to!

166
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:57,500
[panting]

167
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,630
- I'll help you.
- You need to rest

168
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:05,880
until you're healed up.

169
00:10:06,210 --> 00:10:07,250
You're hurt, too.

170
00:10:07,330 --> 00:10:08,670
[grunts]
True.

171
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,710
Just don't push yourself
too hard.

172
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:12,540
Start with kneading.

173
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,920
[ORLAND]
Right.

174
00:10:14,830 --> 00:10:16,630
[KIETH]
Please forgive the intrusion!

175
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:17,960
[panting]

176
00:10:18,290 --> 00:10:21,460
[ELLIOTT] Kieth! Did you come
to check on our injuries?

177
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:24,790
Thanks, but we've got
everything covered here.

178
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,630
Mister Collins!

179
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,170
What are you doing?

180
00:10:29,250 --> 00:10:31,170
I know that Anne
has just been abducted,

181
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:32,920
why are you working right now?

182
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,710
"Why?" Whatever do you mean?

183
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:37,250
Why are none of you
doing anything to help her?

184
00:10:37,380 --> 00:10:39,880
You could search for her!
Or hunt down that fairy!

185
00:10:41,170 --> 00:10:43,080
[stutters] Well,
we thought it was best to leave

186
00:10:43,170 --> 00:10:44,630
all that to the Viscount.

187
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:46,420
That may be,
but why are the rest of you

188
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,500
still doing nothing?

189
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,330
[ELLIOTT]
But we are doing something.

190
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:52,210
No, you should be doing
something for Anne right now!

191
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:53,330
Are you a fool?

192
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:54,830
Why does it seem like
you don't care at all

193
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,380
about what could happen to her?

194
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,670
Is it because
she's not technically

195
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:59,540
an artisan
of the Paige Workshop?

196
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:04,130
[ELLIOTT] Anne isn't an artisan
of the Paige Workshop?

197
00:11:04,210 --> 00:11:06,040
How dare you say that?

198
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,170
Anne is our
Head of Artisans now!

199
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:10,920
You want us to do
something for her?

200
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,630
Do you think we wouldn't go
after her if we could, huh?

201
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:15,960
Listen, if Challe couldn't
defeat that monster,

202
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,040
then what could we do?

203
00:11:17,130 --> 00:11:18,380
- [ORLAND] Elliott!
- The truth is,

204
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:19,960
we're all sugar artisans

205
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:23,210
and we're doing everything we
can possibly do for Anne here.

206
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:26,040
If she comes back to us, don't
you think she'll be unhappy

207
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:28,040
if we haven't made
any progress on our own?

208
00:11:28,130 --> 00:11:29,130
Uh...

209
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:31,380
[ELLIOTT] That's why we're
continuing our work.

210
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:33,960
So tell me,
what should we be doing?

211
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,750
Huh! What's this?

212
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:37,750
Uh... Kieth's here?

213
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,130
That's enough fighting.

214
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:41,750
- He's going to collapse.
- Exactly!

215
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:44,210
The master's representative
should know better than that!

216
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:46,670
You're defiling a holy space.

217
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:48,500
[coughing]

218
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:51,130
[Elliott chuckles]
Sorry about that.

219
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:55,040
Really, I'm the one
who should be sorry.

220
00:11:55,170 --> 00:11:56,830
I knew you'd all accepted Anne,

221
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:59,790
yet I still criticized
your actions.

222
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,960
I'm a traitor
to the Paige Workshop,

223
00:12:02,210 --> 00:12:04,040
so I am in no position
to speak out.

224
00:12:04,130 --> 00:12:05,290
[ELLIOTT]
Listen, Kieth.

225
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,830
The only one who sees it
that way is you.

226
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,960
Huh!

227
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,000
You're not the only reason

228
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,960
this workshop
started to go downhill.

229
00:12:12,170 --> 00:12:14,500
A lot of things had
compounded all at once.

230
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:17,290
It just happened to line up
with you going to Radcliffe.

231
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:19,420
And even if you had come to us,

232
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,500
you wouldn't have gotten
special treatment.

233
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,880
Because that just isn't
the way Mr. Glen operates.

234
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,080
I think Master Radcliffe
cares a lot more

235
00:12:28,170 --> 00:12:29,750
about those things
than we do.

236
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:31,130
That's for sure.

237
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:33,460
So, what did you
come here for, Kieth?

238
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:36,380
Well, I was worried
about Anne, so I thought...

239
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:40,830
No. That isn't all.
I realize now.

240
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:44,920
I always respected
the Paige Workshop

241
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,080
as the place
where my father did his work,

242
00:12:47,460 --> 00:12:49,880
and all along, the only one
who concerned himself

243
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,750
with factions or preferential
treatment was me.

244
00:12:54,130 --> 00:12:56,830
That's why I didn't understand
that you were sincerely doing

245
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:58,500
all of this for Anne's sake.

246
00:13:00,830 --> 00:13:03,420
Till now I've been such a fool,

247
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:06,580
but no longer!

248
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:08,830
I am going to behave
differently!

249
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:12,830
To my father this place
was deeply meaningful.

250
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,540
That's why I wish
for the Paige Workshop

251
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:16,670
to carry on!

252
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:19,250
Would you allow me
to help you with the work?

253
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:21,540
If making sugar confections
will prove helpful

254
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:24,420
to Anne's cause, then I'd
like to lend you a hand!

255
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:25,960
Are you sure though?

256
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:28,670
I don't think your cranky
old headmaster would like it.

257
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:29,880
[chuckles]

258
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,790
I'm impressed, Mithril Lid Pod.

259
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,210
You're working hard as well!

260
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,080
Radcliffe will be fine.

261
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:39,250
Mr. Collins,
I'm ready to receive orders!

262
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:42,750
Welcome aboard.

263
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:53,540
[panting]

264
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:57,710
♪

265
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,830
[horses galloping]

266
00:14:17,710 --> 00:14:18,960
♪

267
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,790
I wonder how everyone is doing.

268
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,460
Poor Challe.

269
00:14:46,330 --> 00:14:47,790
[LAFALLE]
Hello, Anne.

270
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:50,790
My darling little
silver sugar master.

271
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,000
What? Huh?

272
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,750
Wait, what's in there?

273
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,250
Sugar! I would like you
to make confections for me.

274
00:15:02,330 --> 00:15:04,290
I still need to recover
all my strength

275
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:06,040
and there's no better
remedy for that

276
00:15:06,130 --> 00:15:08,080
than the work
of a silver sugar master.

277
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:10,420
[ANNE]
How did you get that?

278
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,670
We had to work so hard
to refine it this year.

279
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:16,250
[LAFALLE]
Shall I tell you?

280
00:15:17,330 --> 00:15:19,670
I refuse!
I want no part of it!

281
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:21,420
You won't help me?

282
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,630
You troublesome child.

283
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,710
But I'm not surprised.

284
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:28,250
You're as useless
as any other human.

285
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:31,580
You do realize
I'll have to kill you for that.

286
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:33,880
Well, it's no matter,
if you die

287
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,920
I'll just go fetch
some other pitiful human

288
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,250
from your little workshop.

289
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:40,170
No, wait!
Please don't hurt anyone else!

290
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:41,460
Huh.

291
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:45,420
In that case, who's going
to make the sugar confections?

292
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:46,540
[exhales]

293
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:49,580
[whimpers]

294
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,330
I'll make them for you.

295
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,250
Just leave the others alone.

296
00:15:54,750 --> 00:15:56,750
[LAFALLE] You should have said
that to start with.

297
00:15:57,420 --> 00:16:00,290
If you obey,
I'll take good care of you.

298
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,670
[ANNA]
Where is Challe right now?

299
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:05,830
[LAFALLE]
I believe he's washing himself.

300
00:16:06,330 --> 00:16:08,920
If you had seen
the state that he was in,

301
00:16:09,210 --> 00:16:11,750
I'm sure the sight
would've turned your stomach.

302
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,500
He's an impressive fairy.

303
00:16:16,290 --> 00:16:18,250
I can see that
he's still hesitant,

304
00:16:18,580 --> 00:16:19,830
but after that's gone,

305
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,250
I can only imagine

306
00:16:21,330 --> 00:16:23,630
how incredible
his swordsmanship will be.

307
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:25,540
[ANNE]
What are you making him do?

308
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:27,920
[LAFALLE]
Oh, nothing too significant.

309
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:34,540
He's simply removing
those who'd stand in my way.

310
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:36,630
What do you mean?

311
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:38,420
Oh, are you worried?

312
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:41,330
Well, I suppose you do
love him, don't you?

313
00:16:42,290 --> 00:16:44,830
To be honest,
if you care about him,

314
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,880
then it's better
if you leave him.

315
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:50,080
You'll be just fine.

316
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:53,420
You can enjoy having him
by your side for a while.

317
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,630
But as soon as you die,

318
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,750
he's going to be left
all alone again,

319
00:16:59,170 --> 00:17:01,040
just as he was before.

320
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:04,750
In order to be happy,
humans and fairies

321
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:06,960
should stay amongst
their own kind.

322
00:17:08,250 --> 00:17:10,250
If you truly want
what's best for Challe,

323
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:11,500
the answer is clear.

324
00:17:11,790 --> 00:17:14,000
You'll let him live
with his fellow fairies

325
00:17:14,290 --> 00:17:16,250
while you gracefully
step aside.

326
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:19,790
The way things are

327
00:17:20,290 --> 00:17:22,460
you will cause him
nothing but sorrow.

328
00:17:23,170 --> 00:17:24,330
[gasps]

329
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:25,880
[exhales]

330
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:29,380
[panting]

331
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,380
[ANNE]
Challe!

332
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,880
Where are you?

333
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:35,540
Huh!

334
00:17:36,290 --> 00:17:37,630
[panting]

335
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:40,170
- In here?
- Hm?

336
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:43,790
[sighs]

337
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,830
[LUSUL]
Oh, I believe I know you!

338
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:48,670
You're the young lady
who gave me life!

339
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:50,580
- Huh?
- It's me!

340
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:53,710
Lusul El Min.
Don't you remember?

341
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,960
♪

342
00:18:00,290 --> 00:18:02,790
You're from back then.
Huh.

343
00:18:03,330 --> 00:18:04,670
What happened to your wing?

344
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:07,580
Oh, no, were you
captured by a human?

345
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:10,000
Actually, I removed my wing

346
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,960
and offered it
to Master Lafalle!

347
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:13,500
[ANNE]
Removed it?

348
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:15,460
You mean
you tore it off yourself?

349
00:18:15,630 --> 00:18:17,630
[LUSUL] Oh, no,
I couldn't do it myself.

350
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,290
It would've been too painful.

351
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:20,790
Luckily, Master Lafalle

352
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:22,420
was kind enough
to do it for me!

353
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:23,960
And for everyone here!

354
00:18:24,170 --> 00:18:26,290
We've all given
one of our wings to him.

355
00:18:26,380 --> 00:18:28,290
To show proof of our loyalty!

356
00:18:29,170 --> 00:18:31,880
[ANNE]
Your loyalty? But what for?

357
00:18:32,630 --> 00:18:35,130
Why would anyone
pledge loyalty to him?

358
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:36,790
He's the new king
of the fairies,

359
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,210
so, of course, we would obey!

360
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:40,960
Under his leadership,
we'll claim our freedom!

361
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:44,000
He made a promise to fight
for the good of all fairies!

362
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,420
We serve him!

363
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,460
Claim your freedom?

364
00:18:48,630 --> 00:18:49,920
[sobbing]

365
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,080
How cruel.

366
00:18:52,710 --> 00:18:54,170
He sold you a lie.

367
00:18:57,250 --> 00:18:58,960
It doesn't make any sense!

368
00:18:59,330 --> 00:19:01,040
Why would he promise you
your freedom

369
00:19:01,130 --> 00:19:02,880
and then take complete
control over you?

370
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:06,210
At that point, he's no
different than a human!

371
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,960
Oh, no.
This is only natural for us.

372
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:13,380
- After all, he's our new king.
- It's not natural!

373
00:19:13,830 --> 00:19:17,000
He's not a king!
He's a fraud! [sobbing]

374
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,670
Why are you crying now?
Are you upset?

375
00:19:19,750 --> 00:19:21,330
[ANNE]
No, I'm furious!

376
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:23,670
There's no reason
he would need your wings!

377
00:19:23,750 --> 00:19:26,170
No king in the world
has the right to take something

378
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:29,580
that beautiful from you,
and a real king wouldn't!

379
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,170
[Anne crying]

380
00:19:31,790 --> 00:19:33,210
[LUSUL]
Beautiful?

381
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:35,540
Beautiful.

382
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,290
[ANNE] How could you not see
how awful that is?

383
00:19:38,710 --> 00:19:41,040
[LUSUL] Does that mean
you're crying for us?

384
00:19:42,210 --> 00:19:45,080
Do you all feel that way?

385
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:47,460
Why is that?

386
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:49,540
- [sobbing]
- footsteps approaching]

387
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:50,830
Hm?

388
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,500
Oh, Challe.

389
00:19:54,330 --> 00:19:56,880
Oh, you're the kind fairy
I met before!

390
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,830
This girl is upset,

391
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,040
but we're not
sure what the problem is.

392
00:20:02,710 --> 00:20:05,420
Not a single one of you
understands why she's angry?

393
00:20:05,630 --> 00:20:06,920
- Hm?
- Hm?

394
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,380
Lusul El Min. You either?

395
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,880
Huh...

396
00:20:12,290 --> 00:20:14,330
I don't. I'm sorry.

397
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:18,670
[CHALLE]
Very well then. Let's go.

398
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:20,920
Wait a minute, please!
Can't you tell us why?

399
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:23,420
I'd like to know
what caused her tears!

400
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:27,630
This human girl
returned my wing.

401
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:30,880
And Lafalle stole it
back for himself.

402
00:20:31,170 --> 00:20:32,790
Think about what that means.

403
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:37,000
[door creaking]

404
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:41,330
[CHALLE]
Are you all right?

405
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:43,630
It's just that,

406
00:20:44,250 --> 00:20:46,460
I don't know the right thing
to do anymore.

407
00:20:47,130 --> 00:20:49,170
♪

